WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.033
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:03.734
We're hanging out
with Allison Williams.

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:05.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:06.901
Go see "M3GAN" this weekend.

00:00:06.901 --> 00:00:09.801
Allison and I are about to play
a singing version

00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:12.100
of "The Whisper Challenge."
-Mm.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:15.567
[ Indistinct whispering ]

00:00:15.567 --> 00:00:17.834
-Whisper Challenge.

00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:19.567
-All right.
Now, here's how this works.

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:21.501
One person puts
on these headphones

00:00:21.501 --> 00:00:22.801
with loud music playing.

00:00:22.801 --> 00:00:24.467
And then the other person
picks up a card,

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:26.634
sings the song lyrics
on the card,

00:00:26.634 --> 00:00:27.767
and the person
wearing headphones

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:29.567
tries to guess
what they just said, okay?

00:00:29.567 --> 00:00:30.968
-Okay.
-All right.

00:00:30.968 --> 00:00:32.133
So, you'll put the headphones --
you can play this at home.

00:00:32.133 --> 00:00:33.434
-I'm going first?
-Yeah. You go first.

00:00:33.434 --> 00:00:34.534
I'll put the song on.
-They can play it at home.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:35.767
-Yeah, you can play it at home.
Sure.

00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:36.801
If you put on headphones,
play it.

00:00:36.801 --> 00:00:38.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:40.067
Whenever Allison --
are you ready for this?

00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:41.501
-I don't know.
Is it going to be really loud?

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:42.834
-Yeah.

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:45.767
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:47.400
-It's really loud.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:48.501
-All right, here we go.

00:00:48.501 --> 00:00:49.868
-I mean, I really
can't hear you.

00:00:49.868 --> 00:00:51.467
-Okay, perfect.

00:00:55.501 --> 00:00:59.000
[ Whispering ]
♪ Well, shake it up, baby, now ♪

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.067
-Did it end with "baby cow"?

00:01:01.067 --> 00:01:02.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:03.400
[ Rimshot ]

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:06.501
-♪ Twist and shout ♪

00:01:06.501 --> 00:01:07.567
-Oh, "Twist and Shout"?

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.868
-Wow! Yes! Yes!
-"Twist and Shout"?

00:01:09.868 --> 00:01:12.033
Wow! That was it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:14.734
-Wow!
-Hey, we're really good.

00:01:14.734 --> 00:01:16.934
-Well, to be fair,
I guessed "baby cow" first.

00:01:16.934 --> 00:01:18.334
-"Baby cow" was good, too.

00:01:18.334 --> 00:01:19.801
-You know that famous pop song
that has "baby cow" in it?

00:01:19.801 --> 00:01:21.234
-"Baby Shark" was big.
-In my --

00:01:21.234 --> 00:01:22.434
By the way, in my Spotify...
-Oh, my God.

00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:24.000
-...it's big.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.000
-Let's write "Baby Cow," and
let's make a zillion dollars.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.067
-That's great.
-Um, all right.

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:28.300
Here's a microphone for you.
-Okay.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:29.567
-I should have used one,
as well.

00:01:29.567 --> 00:01:30.767
All right, here we go.
I'm going to put this on.

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:31.934
-[ Echoing ] Does it do --
will it change it?

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:33.133
Oh. Hello.

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:35.267
Yes. Okay.

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:37.868
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:37.868 --> 00:01:39.567
-[ Clears throat ]

00:01:39.567 --> 00:01:42.133
-♪ You're so vain ♪
-Oh, you started?

00:01:42.133 --> 00:01:43.534
-Yes.
-Sorry.

00:01:43.534 --> 00:01:45.734
-I'm -- This is me starting.
-Here we go.

00:01:45.734 --> 00:01:47.767
-I'm starting.
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:50.767
♪ You're so vain ♪

00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:53.434
-Court -- Court vay?

00:01:53.434 --> 00:01:54.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:57.133
-♪ You're so vain ♪

00:01:57.133 --> 00:02:00.234
-You're so serious.
-Vain.

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:01.868
-You're -- Face facts.
-Vain.

00:02:01.868 --> 00:02:03.667
-Face facts.
-Face facts.

00:02:03.767 --> 00:02:05.133
-Face facts.
-Face facts?

00:02:05.133 --> 00:02:06.601
No.
♪ You're... ♪

00:02:06.601 --> 00:02:07.868
-You.
-♪ So ♪

00:02:07.868 --> 00:02:09.601
-Face -- No, "You so --"

00:02:09.601 --> 00:02:10.901
-You're.
-"You're So Vain?"

00:02:10.901 --> 00:02:14.367
-Yes! Yes!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.033
-♪ Don't you? Don't you? ♪
-Yes!

00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:18.234
-♪ Don't you? ♪
-Yes.

00:02:18.234 --> 00:02:19.701
-Yes.
-Okay, wait, I need these.

00:02:19.701 --> 00:02:21.000
-That song was about me.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.067 --> 00:02:24.200
That's how vain it was.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.367
I was correct --
It was about me.

00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:27.901
Ready? Ready?

00:02:27.901 --> 00:02:29.133
[ Chuckling ] Oh, no.

00:02:29.133 --> 00:02:30.734
Okay.

00:02:30.734 --> 00:02:32.434
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:35.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.667 --> 00:02:39.434
-A-B-C-D-E-F-U.
-I know this one!

00:02:39.434 --> 00:02:41.701
"A-B-C-D-E-F-G"?

00:02:41.701 --> 00:02:42.901
[ Bell dinging ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:42.901 --> 00:02:45.067
"ABCDEFU"!
-Yeah, thank you.

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:47.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.501
♪♪

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:51.300
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:52.467
The -- You got -- You got --

00:02:52.467 --> 00:02:54.767
-I got baby --
-You got baby on the brain.

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:57.834
You're like, "I love this song.
The ABCs?"

00:02:57.834 --> 00:02:59.000
-The amount of --
the amount of --

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:02.200
-"That's my favorite song --
'ABCDEFG.'"

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:03.767
-The amount of pride I felt

00:03:03.767 --> 00:03:06.601
from knowing the alphabet --
so embarrassing.

00:03:06.601 --> 00:03:07.868
-You're like...
-"I know this one!"

00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:09.033
-"I love this song.
We listen to it every day."

00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:11.033
-I love this one.
It's my jam.

00:03:11.033 --> 00:03:12.300
-It's also "Twinkle Twinkle."

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:13.434
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:13.434 --> 00:03:14.501
-All right, here we go.
-Okay.

00:03:14.501 --> 00:03:16.267
-We've got this, bud.
-Oh, my God.

00:03:16.267 --> 00:03:18.501
I'm so embarrassed.
Okay.

00:03:18.501 --> 00:03:20.434
Okay.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:27.234
♪ You, you, you oughta know ♪
-♪ You, you, you ♪

00:03:27.234 --> 00:03:30.567
-♪ Oughta know ♪

00:03:30.567 --> 00:03:32.267
-You are --
you, you, you are a what?

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:33.968
You're an icicle?
-♪ You, you, you ♪

00:03:33.968 --> 00:03:35.667
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:38.434
♪ Oughta know ♪

00:03:38.434 --> 00:03:40.734
-"Heart and Soul"?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.734 --> 00:03:43.400
-♪ You, you, you ♪
"Hot N Cold"?

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.067
-♪ Oughta... ♪

00:03:45.067 --> 00:03:47.367
-Do that part.
After, "You, you, you"...

00:03:47.367 --> 00:03:49.167
-Oughta.
-Hottay.

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:50.367
[ Light laughter ]
[ Rimshot ]

00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:51.634
You're a hottay.

00:03:51.634 --> 00:03:54.601
-You, you, you oughta --
-You are a hottay.

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:56.734
-Oughta.
-Hot dad.

00:03:56.734 --> 00:03:59.000
-Ought--
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.734
-"You're a hot dad."

00:04:00.734 --> 00:04:04.000
"You, you, you are a hot --"
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.801
-You ought to --
-You are --

00:04:05.801 --> 00:04:06.868
Ought.

00:04:06.868 --> 00:04:08.067
"You Oughta Know"!
-Yes!

00:04:08.067 --> 00:04:09.734
[ Bell dinging ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:11.300
Alanis Morissette.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.234
Allison Williams, everybody.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:13.234 --> 00:04:14.467
Her movie, "M3GAN"
is in theaters now.

00:04:14.467 --> 00:04:15.634
Stick around.

00:04:15.634 --> 00:04:16.901
We're talking
to Jerrod Carmichael

